1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:01,163
In 1986,

2
00:00:01,163 --> 00:00:02,410
a Big Mac cost

3
00:00:02,410 --> 00:00:05,560
$1.60 in America.

4
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:06,262
Today,

5
00:00:06,262 --> 00:00:08,730
it costs $6.22.

6
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:09,567
Almost four

7
00:00:09,567 --> 00:00:11,010
times as much.

8
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:12,076
But a dollar from

9
00:00:12,076 --> 00:00:12,904
1986 isn't worth

10
00:00:12,904 --> 00:00:14,307
a dollar today.

11
00:00:14,307 --> 00:00:15,183
So let's adjust

12
00:00:15,183 --> 00:00:16,430
for inflation.

13
00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:17,509
Since 1986,

14
00:00:17,509 --> 00:00:19,008
prices in America

15
00:00:19,008 --> 00:00:20,910
have roughly tripled.

16
00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:21,599
Had the Big Mac

17
00:00:21,599 --> 00:00:22,814
just kept pace,

18
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:23,609
it would cost

19
00:00:23,609 --> 00:00:26,350
about $4.85 today.

20
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:28,240
Until around 2008,

21
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:29,508
the two lines crossed

22
00:00:29,508 --> 00:00:30,810
back and forth.

23
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:31,636
Since then,

24
00:00:31,636 --> 00:00:32,472
the Big Mac has

25
00:00:32,472 --> 00:00:33,560
stayed ahead.

26
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:34,348
Even restaurant

27
00:00:34,348 --> 00:00:34,872
prices,

28
00:00:34,872 --> 00:00:35,713
which rose faster

29
00:00:35,713 --> 00:00:36,605
than average,

30
00:00:36,605 --> 00:00:37,388
would only take

31
00:00:37,388 --> 00:00:38,890
it to $5.59.

32
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:39,646
So the Big Mac

33
00:00:39,646 --> 00:00:40,366
didn't just keep

34
00:00:40,366 --> 00:00:41,640
up with inflation.

35
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:42,540
It beat it,

36
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:44,990
by $1.37 a burger.

37
00:00:44,990 --> 00:00:46,160
Prices tripled.

38
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:47,350
The Big Mac nearly

39
00:00:47,350 --> 00:00:48,360
quadrupled.
